Simple Method Overloading Program in Java :

class Addition {

    void add(int a, int b) {
        System.out.println("Addition of 2 numbers : " + (a + b));
    }

    void add(int a, int b, int c) {
        System.out.println("Addition of 3 numbers : " + (a + b + c));
    }
}

public class Main {

    public static void main(String[] args) {

        Addition obj = new Addition();

        obj.add(10, 20);

        obj.add(10, 20, 30);
    }
}

Output :
Addition of 2 numbers : 30
Addition of 3 numbers : 60

Flow :
obj.add(10,20)
→ calls 2-parameter method
obj.add(10,20,30)
→ calls 3-parameter method

Simple Syntax of Overloading :

void methodName(int a)
void methodName(int a, int b)
void methodName(int a, int b, int c)

Same method name
Different parameters
